Qxc6 85. Qxb4 Qc2 86. Qa5+ Kb2 87. Qb5+ Qb3 88. Qe2+ {"Q-Q7ch" but this is the
only vageuly plausible move} Ka3 {and finally "88.Qb8ch" - whatever that is
supposed to be. A very odd score indeed! Source: Tinsley notebooks} 1/2-1/2

